{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "04DY", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$V \\mapsto V_X$", "MATH_0002": "$V \\to Y$", "MATH_0003": "$V$", "MATH_0004": "$U \\to X$", "MATH_0005": "$U$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{theorem-topological-invariance}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{limits-proposition-affine}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-affine-inside-equivalence}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9182fe83cdc770f723d2cf2752a8756b3c38f3b00d85f410089aec8c2d1c5ae9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:48b98face3ab409216cae48890172d4e8a25454cda715a235feaf6470501c072", "source_text": "In the situation of\nTheorem <REF_0001>\nit is also true that <MATH_0001> induces an equivalence\nbetween those <ACCENT_0001>tale morphisms <MATH_0002> with <MATH_0003> affine and\nthose <ACCENT_0002>tale morphisms <MATH_0004> with <MATH_0005> affine.\nThis follows for example from\nLimits, Proposition <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f3e23bbba55be15a4d405147552a7f7920f164fb65db8aef85f6cceb9d2f1eef", "unit_id": "tag:05YX:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proposition", "parent_tag": "04DY", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0003": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$X_0 \\to X$", "MATH_0002": "$X_\\etale$", "MATH_0003": "$(X_0)_\\etale$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Sh(X_\\etale)$", "MATH_0005": "$\\Sh((X_0)_\\etale)$", "MATH_0006": "$H^q_\\etale(X, \\mathcal{F}) = H^q_\\etale(X_0, \\mathcal{F}|_{X_0})$", "MATH_0007": "$q$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0009": "$X_\\etale$", "OWNARGEND_0001": "]\n\\label{proposition-topological-invariance}\n", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proposition}[", "suffix": "\\end{proposition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ac5c476b2e4c7fab8f99ac775c1c54e385f78d97d17a48b9a6ac4cb4f3fee24c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6b7acad26d33964cc4a5e52c7372b03a7ff4047351d6067035b481e876c56e70", "source_text": "Topological invariance of <ACCENT_0001>tale cohomology<OWNARGEND_0001>Let <MATH_0001> be a universal homeomorphism of schemes\n(for example the closed immersion defined by a nilpotent sheaf of ideals).\nThen\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> the <ACCENT_0002>tale sites <MATH_0002> and <MATH_0003> are isomorphic,\n<STRUCT_0003> the <ACCENT_0003>tale topoi <MATH_0004> and <MATH_0005>\nare equivalent, and\n<STRUCT_0004> <MATH_0006>\nfor all <MATH_0007> and\nfor any abelian sheaf <MATH_0008> on <MATH_0009>.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:db85ef3b04e3027cd5d59a9c44678502c3f346e70b4e4d5d696b9381ece73ca8", "unit_id": "tag:03SI:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04DY", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$X_\\etale \\to (X_0)_\\etale$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{theorem-topological-invariance}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:68d9b6698b5e34da112a7ba6f152b467bc83ad8e391c7b9233072265cf4dcae5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e7d7b7bfcd01b200ec88858b0c77bfe221f34f7b31533be62b5bd18c90edf26a", "source_text": "The equivalence of categories <MATH_0001> is\ngiven by Theorem <REF_0001>. We omit\nthe proof that under this equivalence the <ACCENT_0001>tale coverings correspond.\nHence (1) holds. Parts (2) and (3) follow formally from (1).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6f057f07639c7ea47e4feaeb15336e9442dcecc8daaccf56a6317927999b4196", "unit_id": "tag:03SI:proof"}
